@format 1
@id section-modification.split-selected-section
@title Split selected section
@section Section modification
@area In Split tab
@entry split-dispatch
@summary Modify an existing selected section by shortening its end to the cursor as part of Split; the same operation also creates a new right-hand section and is therefore cross-documented under Section creation.
@related section-modification.common.compass-buttons, section-modification.common.keyboard-shortcuts, section-modification.common.apply-modified-state, section-creation.split-selected-section
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag divide

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias piece = Cadroue.Core.LPiece

[split-dispatch] splitSection dispatch request <input>
~ This starts with splitSection dispatch request.
[Technical explanation]
= The request came from the Split Compass Split button or the currently bound SectionSplit shortcut.
> dispatch-guard

[dispatch-guard] Active Split flow guard <decision>
~ The program checks active Split flow guard.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowShortcutDispatch requires a command-active flow with a loaded spool and active section UI before invoking PFlowSectionDivide @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / splitSection
? "Rejected" > dispatch-rejected
? "Accepted" > editable-check

[dispatch-rejected] Split ignored <output>
~ This path ends with split ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= No section operation is called.

[editable-check] Section editing enabled <decision>
~ The program checks section editing enabled.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionDivide returns when section editing is disabled; otherwise it resets pFlowSegmentFired, chooses the next palette color, and calls LSegmentDivide at the cursor @ flow.PFlowSectionDivide(...)
@ flow.PFlowColorRead(...)
? "Editing disabled" > split-blocked
? "Editing enabled" > divide-plan

[split-blocked] Split blocked <output>
~ This path ends with split blocked.
[Technical explanation]
= Existing section state is unchanged.

[divide-plan] Selected section and interior cursor <decision>
~ The program checks selected section and interior cursor.
[Technical explanation]
- LSegmentDivide asks LPieceDivide for a plan; an active section must exist and the cursor must be strictly greater than its start and strictly less than its end @ segment.LSegmentDivide(...)
@ piece.LPieceDivide(...)
? "No selection or cursor not strictly inside" > split-invalid
? "Valid interior split" > replace-section

[split-invalid] No split modification <output>
~ This path ends with no split modification.
[Technical explanation]
= Existing section state is unchanged and no split log is written.

[replace-section] Replace selected section with two pieces <process>
~ This step handles replace selected section with two pieces.
[Technical explanation]
- Remove the selected LPiece, insert the original piece with LPieceEnd shortened to cursor as the left half, insert a new unnamed right half from cursor to the original end using the new color, and keep the left-half index active @ piece.LPieceDivide(...)
= The shortened left half is the modification covered here; creation of the right half is the Section creation aspect of the same atomic plan.
> map:section-modification.common.apply-modified-state
